{
  "description": "Recorded sink requests and harness events for the harness self-test. Replayed at a live sink receiver over real HTTP by `python -m harness.run --dry`, so the receiver's own parsing is exercised rather than bypassed. The ntfy bodies follow SPEC.md \"Alert shape (normative)\": provenance rides on a line of `message` beginning `riemann-go: `, because the ntfy server discards top-level fields it does not recognize. The write bodies are InfluxDB v2 line protocol.",
